{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Then he commanded.</b> Every one who sits on the throne of the kingdom of Egypt is called, in the Egyptian language, Pharaoh. Now the verse did not state his [personal] name, like Pharaoh Necho (Jeremiah 46:2) — thus is his name in the language of his people; and likewise Pharaoh Hophra (Jeremiah 44:30)." "<b>The one born.</b> An adjectival noun, like גבור שכור (Isaiah 49:26)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved פרע הפרע as Pharaoh Hophra per the Jeremiah 44:30 citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:54.815887197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}